    "title": "Enforce a per-tenant budget",
    "minutes": 6,
    "lessonPath": "/technology/rate-limiting",
    "concept": "What is per-tenant admission control?",
    "summary": "Admission control decides which work can enter a system. Separate tenant budgets keep one customer\u2019s burst from consuming another customer\u2019s allowance.",
    "example": "With a limit of 2, the third request from tenant A is rejected even if tenant B has used none.",
    "takeaway": "Copy counts into a Map and update only accepted requests.",
    "instruction": "Process requests [{id, tenant}] in order, starting from counts. Return {accepted, rejected, counts} using request IDs and a positive integer per-tenant limit. Preserve inputs and safely handle any tenant name.",
    "hint": "Copy counts into a Map and update only accepted requests.",
    "starterFile": "/api/content/technology/rate-limiting/code/code-admit-batch.js",
    "functionName": "admitBatch",
    "tests": [
      {
